### Try these in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (click "Send Request" above each block)

@base = http://localhost:4000/api

### Health check
GET {{base}}/health

### Register the subject first
POST {{base}}/subjects
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "General" }

### MANUAL ENTRY - add a question (number Q101, Q102... is assigned automatically)
POST {{base}}/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "GENERAL", "unit": 1,
  "topic": "Java",
  "subtopic": "Stack",
  "difficulty": "EASY",
  "marks": 2,
  "text": "What is a stack?"
}

### List / filter / search
GET {{base}}/questions?unit=1&topic=java&difficulty=easy

### Get one question (101 or Q101)
GET {{base}}/questions/Q101

### Update
PUT {{base}}/questions/Q101
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "GENERAL", "unit": 1,
  "topic": "Java",
  "subtopic": "Stack",
  "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
  "marks": 5,
  "text": "Explain stack operations with an example."
}

### Delete (soft delete)
DELETE {{base}}/questions/Q101

### Deleted list
GET {{base}}/questions/deleted

### Undo the last delete
POST {{base}}/questions/undo

### Statistics
GET {{base}}/stats

### AUTOMATIC - pick questions by topic / subtopic / marks / difficulty
POST {{base}}/generate/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subject": "GENERAL", "topic": "Java", "subtopic": "Stack", "marks": 2, "difficulty": "EASY", "count": 3 }

### Generate a balanced question paper (unit 0 = all units)
POST {{base}}/papers/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subject": "GENERAL", "unit": 1, "topic": "Java", "totalMarks": 24, "split": { "easy": 40, "medium": 40, "hard": 20 } }